/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   EV FOR ARTISTS — the page, in the four languages the house speaks.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   "EV for Artists" is the programme name and does not translate, in any
   locale, in any position — header, title, metadata, confirmations, documents.

   Three things must say the same thing in every language, because they are
   what an artist decides on: the royalty base (what the percentage is taken
   of), the payment terms (quarterly, 30 days), and the rights language (the
   artist keeps ownership; intake permits internal review only; production
   needs a separate signed agreement). Where a phrase could be read two ways,
   the English is the one the agreement is drafted from.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
